<title>HUNGARY: ABN AMRO's MHB profit surges in 1996.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO's MHB profit surges in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>					Jan-Dec 1996   Jan-Dec 1995</p>
<p>    Operating profit		7,057	vs     1,710</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		  5,801	vs     1,681</p>
<p>    Net interest income	  13,391	vs     8,265</p>
<p>	Interest revenue	   47,975	vs    47,843</p>
<p>	Interest paid		34,584	vs    39,578</p>
<p>    Dividend received		 157	vs	 402</p>
<p>Expenditures on banking</p>
<p>	activity			9,983	vs     8,257</p>
<p>Revenue from other</p>
<p>	banking activity	   22,270	vs    35,273</p>
<p>    Other revenue		  10,082	vs    16,384</p>
<p>Expenditures on other</p>
<p>	banking activity	   20,426	vs    38,283</p>
<p>    Other expenditures	    8,434	vs    12,074</p>
<p>Net income from non-core</p>
<p>	activities			 51 profit vs	29 loss</p>
<p>Revenue from non-core</p>
<p>	  activities		    175		   592</p>
<p>Expenditure on non-core</p>
<p>	  activities		    124	vs	 620</p>
<p>    Net extraordinary income    1,307 loss vs	   0</p>
<p>	Extraordinary revenue     1,396	vs    42,225</p>
<p>	Extraordinary expend.     2,702	vs    42,224</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total	 251,771	vs   246,691</p>
<p>NOTE - Magyar Hitel Bank Rt said the figures were preliminary and were not consolidated. The bank is controlled by ABN AMRO Bank of the Netherlands.</p>
<p>-- BudapesT newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
